			<div class="content" id="post-content-2043655">
									

<p>The FBI wouldn't have a &quot;director of the UIU administrative council&quot; it would be something like &quot;Special Assistant to the Director of Budgeting and Audting Oversite, UIU&quot; or (more likely) &quot;Special Review Board, UIU&quot;.</p>
<p>The rest of it&#8230;isn't on an even keel. Either Keynes doesn't believe in SCPs, in which case he should be trying to deny funding for people hurting themselves chasing <em>fairy tales</em>, or he DOES and funding shouldn't be an issue.</p>
<p>In the end, the only reason for a Federal agency to keep funding something like this is is because it's a rider of something larger and &quot;pork barrel spending&quot; - They can't actually deny them the money (without getting an audit upon their head) but they don't have to make it pleasant - which you do show quite well.</p>

							</div>

								
