			<div class="content" id="post-content-2044386">
									

<p>I appreciate the criticism. But just to make a few things clear (Numbered for the sake of convenience):</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Less&nbsp;stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Point #2: The panel is not fully UIU, per say. Like i've said before, they are meant to be a bad imitation of the O5 council. They do understand what their objectives are, but, not receiving much respect, they attempt to isolate themselves from the rest of the group.</p>
<p>Points #5, 10 and 12: The official with the briefcase is <em>not</em> from UIU. He's from the FBI Resource Planning Office (Yay, I learned something!). I meant to convey that through Keynes' 'nod'. Sorry if that was too unclear.</p>
<p>I think Point #8: I just meant that he had a black suit and tie. He is referring to the Men in Black in the UIU orientation. For some reason, I had never noticed that when I was writing it.</p>
</div>
